.TH CHTTPSVR_REQ_METHOD 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_req_method \- return the HTTP method of a request
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

chttp_method_t chttpsvr_req_method(const chttpsvr_req *req);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns the HTTP method of req as a chttp_method_t enum value.  The
value is always one of the seven real methods (CHTTP_GET, CHTTP_POST,
CHTTP_PUT, CHTTP_DELETE, CHTTP_PATCH, CHTTP_HEAD and CHTTP_OPTIONS);
the function never returns CHTTP_ANY, even when the route that matched
was registered with CHTTP_ANY.

A request whose method the server does not recognize at all (a WebDAV
verb such as PROPFIND, a verb such as TRACE or CONNECT, or a custom
verb) never reaches any handler, including one registered with
CHTTP_ANY: the server rejects it with 501 Not Implemented before
routing runs (see the notes on CHTTP_ANY in
chttpsvr_register_handler(3)).  This is what makes "always one of the
seven real methods" a complete guarantee rather than just the common
case.

The function returns CHTTP_GET when req is NULL.  Most other request
accessors return NULL for a NULL req, but chttp_method_t is an integer
enum with no sentinel value, so this one cannot.  If req can be NULL,
check for NULL before calling this function.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_req_path (3),
.BR chttpsvr_req_header (3)
